    {
     "type": "application",
     "title": "Train Deliberately, Perform Automatically",
     "content": "1. **Do all your deliberate correction before performance, never during.** Rehearse, analyze video, get coaching feedback — but treat that as strictly separate from the moment of actual execution.\n\n2. **Build a short pre-performance ritual** — a consistent physical or mental cue (a breath pattern, a phrase, a stretch) that signals 'aiming is done, now I release control to the trained system.'\n\n3. **Pick one external focus point during execution** instead of monitoring your own body — a sports-psychology technique called an external focus cue, like watching the target instead of narrating your own arm motion, which measurably outperforms internal self-monitoring in skill research.\n\n4. **If you notice yourself narrating your own performance mid-task, don't fight it directly** — gently redirect attention back to the external focus point or the next immediate action, rather than trying to consciously fix the narration.\n\n5. **Save all analysis for afterward.** Debrief, review, and adjust your training only once the performance is fully over — matching both Maltz's aim/release split and the flow research on how skilled performance actually holds together under pressure.",
     "visual": {
      "type": "diagram",
      "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" class=\"lesson-visual\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" rx=\"16\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/>\n<text x=\"550\" y=\"68\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-size=\"32\" font-weight=\"bold\">AIM CONSCIOUSLY, RELEASE FULLY</text>\n<text x=\"550\" y=\"108\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"19\" font-weight=\"normal\">Five steps to flow-compatible performance</text>\n<rect x=\"80\" y=\"200\" width=\"940\" height=\"140\" rx=\"16\" fill=\"#6366f1\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"2\" opacity=\"0.08\"/>\n<text x=\"116\" y=\"242\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-size=\"21\" font-weight=\"bold\">1. Correct only before performance</text>\n<text x=\"116\" y=\"276\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"normal\">Never mid-execution</text>\n<rect x=\"80\" y=\"364\" width=\"940\" height=\"140\" rx=\"16\" fill=\"#8b5cf6\" stroke=\"#8b5cf6\" stroke-width=\"2\" opacity=\"0.08\"/>\n<text x=\"116\" y=\"406\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#8b5cf6\" font-size=\"21\" font-weight=\"bold\">2. Use a pre-performance ritual</text>\n<text x=\"116\" y=\"440\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"normal\">A cue that signals \"release now\"</text>\n<rect x=\"80\" y=\"528\" width=\"940\" height=\"140\" rx=\"16\" fill=\"#0ea5e9\" stroke=\"#0ea5e9\" stroke-width=\"2\" opacity=\"0.08\"/>\n<text x=\"116\" y=\"570\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#0ea5e9\" font-size=\"21\" font-weight=\"bold\">3. Pick one external focus point</text>\n<text x=\"116\" y=\"604\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"normal\">Not your own body or voice</text>\n<rect x=\"80\" y=\"692\" width=\"940\" height=\"140\" rx=\"16\" fill=\"#10b981\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"2\" opacity=\"0.08\"/>\n<text x=\"116\" y=\"734\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-size=\"21\" font-weight=\"bold\">4. Redirect, don’t fight, narration</text>\n<text x=\"116\" y=\"768\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"normal\">Back to the external focus point</text>\n<rect x=\"80\" y=\"856\" width=\"940\" height=\"140\" rx=\"16\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\" stroke-width=\"2\" opacity=\"0.08\"/>\n<text x=\"116\" y=\"898\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" font-size=\"21\" font-weight=\"bold\">5. Debrief only afterward</text>\n<text x=\"116\" y=\"932\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"normal\">Analysis is a post-performance task</text>\n</svg>",
      "caption": "A five-step protocol for trusting the trained mechanism"
     }
    }
